      <p class="text-gray-300">Cloudzy (formerly RouterHosting) is an independent self-funded cloud provider headquartered in Dubai, UAE, operating continuously since 2008 — 18 years without acquisition or VC funding. The pitch is straightforward and unusual at the $2.48/mo entry tier: AMD EPYC CPUs, DDR5 memory, pure NVMe storage, and 40 Gbps networking on every single plan. The provider serves 122,000+ developers and businesses across 13 datacenters (NA, EU, APAC), accepts Monero (XMR) directly, and publishes a 99.95% uptime SLA with a 14-day unconditional money-back guarantee.</p>
